<PageLayout title="Roadmap — TotalRecalls" description="What TotalRecalls does today, what is planned, and what is deliberately not planned." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Roadmap" }]}>
  <h1>Roadmap</h1>
  <p>Available today, in progress, and deliberately not planned. This page is a design statement, not a schedule — nothing here carries a date, because a one-person project that misses invented dates is worse than one that does not publish them.</p>

  <h2>Available today — version 1.0.0</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Eight providers</strong>: ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral and Qwen Chat.</li>
    <li><strong>Markdown and JSON</strong> for every conversation, with provider-specific metadata and web-search results preserved.</li>
    <li><strong>Per-conversation and bulk downloads</strong> into a folder structure you own.</li>
    <li><strong>A Free Tier</strong> — three providers and up to five conversations per provider — so the app can be tested on real chats before paying.</li>
    <li><strong>Windows 10 and 11, 64-bit.</strong> No installation, no account, no telemetry.</li>
    <li><strong>Smart Search Engine (SSE)</strong> — plain-English search across your downloaded archive, running on your PC. Available as a Pro add-on or in the Pro + SSE bundle.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Planned — with design notes</h2>
  <p>Each of these has a page explaining what it would do and what the open question is:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/previews/rag-containers/">RAG containers</a> — a portable knowledge base for other local tools.</li>
    <li><a href="/previews/multi-device-memory/">Multi-device memory</a> — merge archives across your machines.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Considering</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Code signing for portable ZIP.</strong> The official Microsoft Store release is certified with zero security prompts. We are evaluating EV code signing for the direct portable ZIP release.</li>
    <li><strong>macOS and Linux.</strong> The download logic is not Windows-specific, but the embedded sign-in windows and the packaging are.</li>
    <li><strong>RAG containers and multi-device memory</strong> — both have design notes below.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deliberately not planned</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A subscription. The app is a one-time purchase.</li>
    <li>Hosting your conversations. Nothing is uploaded, so there is nothing to host.</li>
    <li>An account system. You sign in to your providers, not to us.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>If something on this page matters to your workflow, say so at <a href="mailto:contact@totalrecalls.app">contact@totalrecalls.app</a>. Explaining how you would use a feature carries more weight than a vote.</p>
</PageLayout>
